ids/semi-solids when BOTH sides explicitly specify different numbers (e.g. requested 15ml drops vs candidate writes 5ml drops).\n60:      - Conflicting injection pack count when explicitly different (e.g. requested 3 ampoules vs candidate writes 1 ampoule).\n61: \n62: SCHEMA:\n63: Return ONLY a valid JSON object matching this schema:\n64: {\n65:   \"results\": [\n66:     {\n67:       \"case_id\": \"string\",\n68:       \"status\": \"match\" | \"review\",\n69:       \"item_id\": \"string (the matching candidate ID)\",\n70:       \"reason\": \"string (Arabic explanation when review, otherwise empty string)\"\n71:     }\n72:   ]\n73: }\n74: \n75: CRITICAL RULES FOR RESPONSE:\n76: - ONLY include cases that are \"match\" or \"review\".\n77: - DO NOT return cases that are \"no_match\" (any omitted case_id is automatically considered no_match).\n78: - DO NOT return markdown blocks (no ```json). Return ONLY the raw JSON starting with { and ending with }.\n79: \"\"\"\n80: \n81: class FastCoordinator:\n82:     def __init__(self, config: Config):\n83:         self.config = config\n84: \n85:     def process(self, shortage_items: list[dict], warehouse_data: dict[str, list[dict]]) -> dict:\n86:         unique_shortages = {}\n87:         for item in shortage_items:\n88:             name = item.get(\"item_name_raw\", \"\")\n89:             if name and name not in unique_shortages:\n90:                 unique_shortages[name] = item\n91:                 \n92:         deduped_shortages = list(unique_shortages.values())\n93: \n94:         print(f\"\\n{'='*60}\")\n95:         print(f\"[FAST ENGINE] Starting Match: {len(shortage_items)} raw -> {len(deduped_shortages)} UNIQUE shortages x {len(warehouse_data)} warehouses\")\n96:         print(f\"{'='*60}\\n\")\n97: \n98:         all_warehouse_results = {}\n99:         found_in = {}\n100: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":4533,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T10:10:16Z","thinking":"If the provided trade brand name differs substantially from the reference brand or its generic equivalent, a \"no_match\" status is essential. Distinguishing between closely related brand names requires careful comparison. The objective is to identify instances where the names are distinctly different, ensuring the correct determination of \"no_match.\"\n\n\nExamining the code, known \"look-alike\" brand pairs are explicitly flagged as \"no_match\". Specifically, checking if both brand names from a distinct pair are present in the compared items. Also, if brand similarity score, `b_sim`, falls below a threshold (65), a \"no_match\" is returned. It's crucial to evaluate the `b_sim` score for specific pairs like `جرانتريل` and `جرانتيل` to assess the logic's behavior. The code extracts brand tokens from names before comparing, indicating a word-based matching approach.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python -c \\\"\\nfrom rapidfuzz import fuzz\\nfrom src.fast_match.search import extract_brand_tokens\\n\\npairs = [\\n    ('جرانتريل', 'جرانتيل'),\\n    ('امبوفير', 'اميفير'),\\n    ('ديباكين', 'ديبيكان'),\\n    ('امبوفير امبول', 'اميفير امبول')\\n]\\nfor p1, p2 in pairs:\\n    b1 = extract_brand_tokens(p1)\\n    b2 = extract_brand_tokens(p2)\\n    ratio = fuzz.ratio(b1, b2)\\n    print(f'{b1} vs {b2} -> ratio={ratio}')\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"d:\\\\AI_Engineer\\\\Pharmacy-agy\"","IsDaemon":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Checking brand tokens ratio\"","toolSummary":"\"Check fuzz ratio for pairs\""}}]}
