{"step_index":4632,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T10:14:30Z","thinking":"The current regex uses word boundaries (`\\b`), preventing matches on strings like \"4/30\" within \"زانوجليد4/30اقراص\". Removing `\\b` or replacing it with character class `(?:^|[^\\d/])` on both sides should fix it. However, a slash could also be part of a price or other ratio, not just a date. Considering the warehouse context, the simplest approach might be to use the simpler regex `(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?\\/\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)` without the surrounding character restrictions.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Test improved regex for slash strength\",\"UserFacing\":false}","CodeContent":"\"import re\\n\\npattern = re.compile(r'(?:^|[^\\\\d/])(\\\\d+(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?\\\\/\\\\d+(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?)(?:[^\\\\d/]|$)')\\n\\ntest_strings = [\\n    'زانوجليد4/30اقراص س ج',\\n    'زانوجليد 4/30 اقراص',\\n    'زانوچيلد 4 مج اقراص/باكت 60', # has اقراص/باكت (no slash between numbers)\\n    'فالسارتان 160/12.5 مجم',\\n    'كابوتن 25 مجم'\\n]\\n\\nfor s in test_strings:\\n    m = pattern.search(s)\\n    val = m.group(1) if m else None\\n    print(f\\\"'{s}' -> {val}\\\")\\n\"","Description":"\"Test improved regex\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\kakak\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a\\\\scratch\\\\test_slash.py\"","toolAction":"\"Writing test_slash.py\"","toolSummary":"\"Create test_slash.py\""}}]}
